{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1373842-soul-magic","id":1373842,"title":"Soul Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-09T22:09:21-07:00","id":1373842,"title":"Soul Magic","content":"I was thinking about what else a Death mage could use his dominion over souls for beyond stealing, storing, and consuming them. This is what I came up with, based off the assumption that Willpower is a manifestation of the soul, particularly the Mind portion there-of. One of the themes of these spells is that the caster leans on his soul to achieve greater effect but at risk of soul damage if whatever he's pouring his heart and soul into fails anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Soulfire<br /> Death 3<br /> Perfecting<br /> The mage stokes the soul of the subject and suffusing their being with the terrible flames of will. <br /> The target gains dots of willpower equal to the potency of the spell, to a limit of what the target could achieve with maximum Resolve and Composure. A willpower enhanced roll that results in no successes causes the subject receiving a negative Condition from the strain on their soul, though this can be contested by the Death 4 Inviolate Soul attainment. <br /> +1 Reach: Instead of +3 dice, spending willpower grants a bonus equal to willpower dots. Doing so causes the target's nimbus to flair as if casting a spell, with a bonus to their effective gnosis equal to potency<br /> +1 Reach: By spending a mana the mage may exceed maximum attributes<br /> +1 Reach: By spending a mana when casting this spell, the mage allows the subject to spend a point of willpower to enhance the Potency of a Legacy attainments by 1 per 2 dice the point of willpower would have granted.<br /> .<br /> Soulcutter<br /> Death 4<br /> Patterning<br /> The subject vanishes, a cut appears, and then the subject reappears along the path of the cut. Though this might appear to be an anime-esque slicing dash, in truth it is a spell of transformation. The subject becomes the act of cutting, not the kinetic act of swinging a blade, but the entropic act of destructive severance. If there can be said to be a blade it is the subject's own soul enacting their will upon the world. Because of this the spell determines the accuracy of the attack and the distance/size it traverses, but the lethal damage weapon rating of the attack is determined by willpower dots of the subject. The subject may reflexively spend a point of willpower to avoid cutting undesired targets in their path, including after the discovery of a supernatural defense but before contesting against it. If the subject strikes a target but is successfully rebuffed to deal no damage (by armor for instance), the subject receiving a negative Condition from the strain on their soul, though this can be contested by the Death 4 Inviolate Soul attainment.<br /> +1 Reach: By spending a mana the subject deals aggravated damage and ignores damage reduction from mundane armor.<br /> +1 Reach: the cut only affects souled entities and inflicts negative soul-based Tilts as it damages the soul <br /> +1 Reach: for the duration of the spell, the cut inflicted by this spell cuts the platonic form of what the victims SHOULD be. Magic less then Making can only fuse together the cut as an act of transformation, not healing or mending. Matter 2 Shaping would be able to put together the parts of a cut vase, but a subsequent casting of Matter 3 Alter Integrity would &quot;fix&quot; it back into being in multiple parts <br /> +2 Reach: the cut inflicted by this spell cuts the platonic form with a Lasting duration<br /> <br /> Soulbleed<br /> Death 2<br /> Ruling<br /> The subject's soul overflows and seeps out to suffuse the secondary targets of this spell. If the subject is a supernatural entity, this inflicts their nimbus tilt or equivalent on the secondary targets. The subject gains constant awareness of the locations of the secondary targets and may reflexively spend willpower points to aid or hinder a secondary target's roll. Furthermore, the spell grants the 9-again quality to teamwork rolls between the secondary targets and the subject. If one of the secondary targets successfully attacks the subject, the subject receiving a negative Condition as their soul is pitted against itself, though this can be contested by the Death 4 Inviolate Soul attainment. The same can also happen to a secondary target as the subject's soul presses down overbearingly on their own if they dramatically fail a roll affected by the subject's willpower.<br /> +1 reach: teamwork between the subject and the secondary targets uses the 8-again quality.<br /> +1 reach: the subject may divide the benefit or malus of their spent willpower point between multiple secondary targets.<br /> +2 teach: all secondary targets receive the full benefit or malus of the spent willpower point.<br /> <br /> Soulplate<br /> Death 3<br /> Weaving<br /> The protective layers of the target's soul that defend against soul-loss expand outwards and becomes a physically manifest armor that turns aside harm by sheer force of will. The target gains ballistic and general armor equal to their willpower dots and a Withstand equal to their willpower dots against more esoteric effects directly affecting him, even those of Abyssal entities. The armor formed by this spell is BLATENTLY obvious and supernatural and the potency of this spell contests attempts to conceal it. As with other soul-based effects, should the target's soulplate be overcome the subject receiving a negative Condition from the strain on their soul, though this can be contested by the Death 4 Inviolate Soul attainment.<br /> +1 reach: the soulplate's form is mutable and the subject can manifest it as extra limbs with the normal strength and dexterity of the caster. The limbs do not grant extra actions per turn, but once per turn the subject can reflexively convert up to Potency points of armor into increasing both the strength and dexterity of the limbs, to a maximum of willpower dots. Or reflexively convert back limb attributes into armor. If the subject wishes, the limbs can be formed holding 0L melee weapons.<br /> +1 reach: the target can perform the reflexive conversions twice a turn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}